# OpenAPI moves with the HTTP surface

A response the API can produce that Swagger UI does not show is a bug, and is tested like one.

When a file matching these globs changes, the **same reply** must also:

| Change | Same-reply update |
|---|---|
| New or changed route | `#[OA\...]` on the action + `docs/openapi.json` dump |
| New or changed request DTO field | request schema / example on the DTO or `#[OA\RequestBody]` |
| New or changed response field or status | `#[OA\Response]` or schema class + dump |
| Example / summary / description only | dump `docs/openapi.json` (snapshot test will fail otherwise) |
| Docs command or `/api/doc` route | `docs/agent/COMMANDS.md` |

Every `WebTestCase` request is followed by `assertResponseIsDocumented($client)`.
Regenerate: `docker compose exec -T app bin/console nelmio:apidoc:dump --format=json > docs/openapi.json`.
Gates: `OpenApiCoverageTest`, `OpenApiSnapshotTest` (ordinary phpunit, not a separate command).
